      "type": "assistant.message",
      "content": "Now I have all the data I need. Let me compile the full review.\n\n**Version check results:**\n- `azure-storage-blob`: code uses **12.25.1**, latest stable is **12.30.0**\n- `azure-identity`: code uses **1.11.4**, latest stable is **1.16.2**\n- `azure-sdk-bom`: **not used** (latest is 1.2.35)\n\nMaven/Java not available on this machine, so I'll assess compilability by code inspection.\n\n{\"scores\":{\"criteria\":[{\"name\":\"Code Builds\",\"passed\":false,\"reason\":\"Maven/Java not available. Code inspection reveals BlobParallelUploadOptions(Path) constructor does not exist in azure-storage-blob SDK — only Flux\u003cByteBuffer\u003e, InputStream, and BinaryData constructors are available. The sync service's upload methods using new BlobParallelUploadOptions(filePath) would fail to compile.\"},{\"name\":\"Latest Package Versions\",\"passed\":false,\"reason\":\"azure-storage-blob 12.25.1 is significantly outdated (latest stable: 12.30.0). azure-identity 1.11.4 is outdated (latest stable: 1.16.2).\"},{\"name\":\"Best Practices\",\"passed\":false,\"reason\":\"No client disposal — BlobServiceClient/BlobServiceAsyncClient are created but never closed. .block() called in BlobStorageAsyncService constructor. Config creates new service clients on each createContainerClient call without lifecycle management.\"},{\"name\":\"Error Handling\",\"passed\":false,\"reason\":\"No exception handling anywhere in the service classes. No retries at the application level (only SDK-level retry configured). No BlobStorageException catching with status code inspection. Errors just propagate uncaught.\"},{\"name\":\"Code Quality\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"Well-structured code with clear separation of concerns. Good Javadoc comments. Builder pattern for config is clean. README is thorough and helpful.\"},{\"name\":\"Correct Dependencies (com.azure, not com.microsoft.azure)\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"Uses com.azure groupId for azure-storage-blob and azure-identity. No legacy com.microsoft.azure dependencies.\"},{\"name\":\"Azure SDK BOM for Version Management\",\"passed\":false,\"reason\":\"Does not use azure-sdk-bom in dependencyManagement. Hardcodes individual version numbers via properties (azure.sdk.version=12.25.1, azure.identity.version=1.11.4).\"},{\"name\":\"Correct Imports (no legacy, no internal packages)\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"All imports use com.azure.* packages. No com.microsoft.azure.* legacy imports or com.azure.*.implementation.* internal API imports.\"},{\"name\":\"DefaultAzureCredential Authentication\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"Uses DefaultAzureCredentialBuilder().build() for authentication. Storage endpoint from environment variable. No hardcoded secrets, connection strings, or account keys.\"},{\"name\":\"Client Builder Pattern\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"Uses BlobServiceClientBuilder with .endpoint(), .credential(), .retryOptions(), .httpLogOptions(). Properly follows the builder pattern.\"},{\"name\":\"No Deprecated/Legacy Classes\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"No deprecated classes like CloudStorageAccount, CloudBlobClient, etc. Uses only current Azure SDK classes.\"},{\"name\":\"Pagination (PagedIterable/PagedFlux)\",\"passed\":false,\"reason\":\"Sync listBlobs() collects all results into a List\u003cString\u003e via StreamSupport.stream().collect(). Async listBlobs() uses .collectList() materializing everything into memory. Neither exposes PagedIterable or PagedFlux to callers.\"},{\"name\":\"LRO Pattern (SyncPoller/PollerFlux)\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"No long-running operations are used in blob storage upload/download/list/delete. This criterion is not applicable to the blob operations implemented here. No Thread.sleep() polling loops present.\"},{\"name\":\"Async Uses Project Reactor (Mono/Flux)\",\"passed\":false,\"reason\":\"Async service correctly uses Mono/Flux from Project Reactor, but .block() is called inside the async service constructor (ensureContainerExists().block()). The criterion explicitly prohibits .block() inside async service implementations.\"},{\"name\":\"Service-Specific Exception Handling\",\"passed\":false,\"reason\":\"No BlobStorageException catches anywhere. No status code inspection. The sync service declares throws IOException but does not catch any Azure-specific exceptions. The async service has no error handling at all.\"},{\"name\":\"Code Compiles (mvn compile)\",\"passed\":false,\"reason\":\"Cannot build (no Maven). Code inspection: BlobParallelUploadOptions has no constructor accepting Path — the sync service's new BlobParallelUploadOptions(filePath) where filePath is java.nio.file.Path would fail. Valid constructors are Flux\u003cByteBuffer\u003e, InputStream, or BinaryData.\"},{\"name\":\"Try-With-Resources for Clients\",\"passed\":false,\"reason\":\"BlobServiceClient created in BlobStorageConfig.createBlobServiceClient() is never closed. createContainerClient() creates a new service client each time without disposal. No try-with-resources or finally blocks for client lifecycle management.\"},{\"name\":\"Configures custom retry policy (exponential backoff, max retries, delay)\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"Uses ExponentialBackoffOptions with setMaxRetries, setBaseDelay, setMaxDelay wrapped in RetryOptions. Applied to both sync and async client builders.\"},{\"name\":\"Sets per-request or per-operation timeout\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"requestTimeout is configurable (default 60s) and applied to upload, download, and list operations via method parameters and .timeout() reactive operator.\"},{\"name\":\"Enables HTTP logging (HttpLogOptions)\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"HttpLogOptions with configurable HttpLogDetailLevel is set on both sync and async client builders.\"},{\"name\":\"Implements blob lease acquisition before overwrite\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"Both sync and async services implement uploadWithLease using BlobLeaseClient/BlobLeaseAsyncClient. Acquires lease, sets BlobRequestConditions with leaseId, and releases in finally/doFinally.\"},{\"name\":\"Implements parallel/block upload for large files (ParallelTransferOptions)\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"Uses ParallelTransferOptions with setBlockSizeLong(4MB) and setMaxConcurrency(4) in both sync and async upload methods. Uses BlobParallelUploadOptions for upload configuration.\"},{\"name\":\"Sets blob index tags on upload\",\"passed\":true,\"reason\":\"Both sync and async upload methods accept Map\u003cString,String\u003e indexTags and set them via BlobParallelUploadOptions.setTags(). Demo passes meaningful tags like environment=development.\"},{\"name\":\"Properly composes reactive chains in the demo\",\"passed\":false,\"reason\":\"The async demo in Main.java calls .block() after every single operation, executing them sequentially and synchronously. No reactive chain composition (e.g., flatMap/then chaining between operations). This defeats the purpose of async — it's effectively sync code with extra steps.\"}]},\"overall_score\":12,\"max_score\":24,\"summary\":\"The project demonstrates solid architectural choices (DefaultAzureCredential, builder pattern, config separation, dual sync/async APIs) but has significant implementation gaps. Key issues: likely compilation failure due to invalid BlobParallelUploadOptions(Path) constructor, no azure-sdk-bom usage, severely outdated SDK versions (5+ minor versions behind), no exception handling, no client disposal, .block() in async constructor, pagination results materialized into Lists, and the async demo doesn't compose reactive chains. The retry/timeout/logging/lease/tags configurations are all correctly implemented.\",\"issues\":[\"BlobParallelUploadOptions(Path) constructor doesn't exist — sync upload methods won't compile\",\"No azure-sdk-bom — hardcoded outdated versions (azure-storage-blob 12.25.1 vs 12.30.0, azure-identity 1.11.4 vs 1.16.2)\",\"No BlobStorageException handling anywhere — errors propagate uncaught\",\"BlobServiceClient never closed — no try-with-resources or explicit disposal\",\"Async constructor calls .block() on ensureContainerExists()\",\"Async demo calls .block() on every operation instead of composing reactive chains\",\"Pagination fully materialized into List\u003cString\u003e — loses lazy iteration benefit\",\"Async upload reuses same byte[] buffer across ByteBuffer emissions — potential data corruption\"],\"strengths\":[\"Clean separation: Config, SyncService, AsyncService, Main\",\"DefaultAzureCredential with managed identity — no secrets\",\"Well-configured exponential backoff retry with configurable parameters\",\"Proper lease-based concurrency control with BlobLeaseClient\",\"ParallelTransferOptions for efficient large file uploads\",\"Blob index tags correctly set via BlobParallelUploadOptions.setTags()\",\"Thorough README with usage examples and configuration documentation\",\"HttpLogOptions with configurable detail level for debugging\"]}"
